                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7726b883-5dfa-3a35-b9d3-4c7c7e5bcc12",
                        "entry_id": "e1a61d37-2952-3815-a582-71ac5d42ca58",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A group of nymphs who tend a blissful garden filled with trees that grew golden apples in a far western corner of the world, located in Libya or the Atlas Mountains in North Africa at the edge of the encircling Oceanus; they are said to be the daughters of Hesperus."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Greek",
                            "plural",
                            "plural-only"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6510802a-cde9-3e60-8244-a6a3515702bf",
                        "entry_id": "e1a61d37-2952-3815-a582-71ac5d42ca58",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The garden of the Hesperides."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Greek",
                            "plural",
                            "plural-only"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "89fe04e2-58bb-380e-acad-b6e84e27b8f2",
                        "entry_id": "e1a61d37-2952-3815-a582-71ac5d42ca58",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A paradisaical land of plenty, especially one in the far West."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "plural",
                            "plural-only"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "92b07bf0-22db-428e-8140-b1e266f1a5ae",
                                "sense_id": "89fe04e2-58bb-380e-acad-b6e84e27b8f2",
                                "text": "Inclinations no leſs vigorous have of late been obſerved in Europe, but with more ſucceſs; who not being bounded by Herculean Bars, paſt ſo far through (till then) the unmeaſured Atlantick, that they lighted upon a new World, a flouriſhing Heſperides, Regions whoſe Sands were Gold, Earth Plate, and Rivers Silver, a Paradice extended to the Arctick and Antarctick Circles, with ſeveral other Countries and Iſlands that reach almoſt the utmoſt latitude of either Poles, out-ſhining all the Fables of Antiquity, and boldeſt Tales of their Poetick Dreams; […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
